---
// FAQSection.astro - Common Questions section
---

<!-- FAQ Section -->
<section class="py-24 px-4 sm:px-6 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-50 to-white">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-12" data-aos="fade-up">
      <h2 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Common Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        Operational and clinical questions — answered directly
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-4" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="100">
      <!-- FAQ 1 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            How quickly can we start receiving assignments?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              You could be receiving patients in as little as 2-3 weeks. Here's
              why it's so fast: Our digital onboarding system lets you review
              and sign everything online in about 15 minutes—no paperwork, no
              lawyers, no delays. The self-service portal walks you through each
              step. The 2-3 week timeline? That's just for standard
              credentialing that every network requires. But unlike the old days
              of paper contracts and phone tag, your part is done in minutes,
              not weeks. Sign today, start credentialing tomorrow, receive
              assignments in weeks.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 20 20">
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>Average time to first patient: 2-3 weeks</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 2 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            What volume increase should we expect?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Our AnciCare partners typically saw 20-40% volume increases. With
              USRad, we're targeting similar results using the same proven
              demand routing model that delivered 168,000+ patient visits.
              Results vary by market, available appointment slots, and pricing
              competitiveness.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4">
              <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
                <strong>Pro tip:</strong> Centers that dedicate specific time blocks
                to USRad patients typically see the highest volume increases.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 3 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            Are there any costs to join USRad?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              No. Just like AnciCare, joining USRad is completely free for
              qualified centers. No setup fees, no monthly charges, no hidden
              costs. We only succeed when you succeed — our revenue comes from
              successfully routing patient assignments to your center.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
                <svg
                  class="w-8 h-8 text-green-600 mx-auto mb-1"
                  fill="currentColor"
                  viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                >
                  <path
                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                    clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-800">$0 Setup</p>
              </div>
              <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-lg p-3 text-center">
                <svg
                  class="w-8 h-8 text-green-600 mx-auto mb-1"
                  fill="currentColor"
                  viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                >
                  <path
                    fill-rule="evenodd"
                    d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                    clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
                </svg>
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-green-800">$0 Monthly</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
      <!-- FAQ 4 — anchor target from ReferralWorkflow -->
      <details
        id="physician-order"
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="150"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            Does a valid physician order come through before a patient is
            scheduled?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Yes — always. USRad requires a valid physician order before any
              patient is scheduled at your facility. During our verification
              step, we confirm the ordering physician, the prescribed exam type,
              and patient eligibility. No order, no appointment. This is
              non-negotiable in our process and mirrors the clinical intake
              standards your center already operates under.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-[#003087]">
              <svg
                class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
                fill="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              >
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
              </svg>
              <span>Physician order verified before every scheduling event</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 5 -->
      <details
        id="data-handling"
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="200"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            How is patient data handled between USRad and our center?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Patient information handling requirements are addressed in the
              onboarding agreement between USRad and your center. Patient data
              is transmitted through a secure portal and limited to what your
              center needs to schedule and perform the study. Your center never
              handles USRad member financial data, and USRad never accesses your
              clinical records or systems.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 6 -->
      <details
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="250"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            Does joining USRad affect our existing payer contracts?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              No. Every assignment USRad routes is funded before it reaches
              you — USRad secures the funding and pays your center directly.
              Nothing is billed through your existing payer relationships. There
              is no overlap with your insurance contracts, no balance billing,
              and no claims filing on your end. Your payer agreements remain
              completely independent.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
              <svg
                class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
                fill="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              >
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
              </svg>
              <span
                >Zero impact on existing payer contracts or credentialing</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 7 -->
      <details
        id="no-show-policy"
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="300"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            What happens if a USRad patient no-shows?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Funding is secured before the appointment is confirmed at your
              facility. In the rare case of a no-show, your center is not
              exposed to a collections situation. The appointment slot simply
              becomes available again.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 8 -->
      <details
        id="contract-terms"
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="350"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            What are the contract terms and length of commitment?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              Contract terms are provided during the digital onboarding process
              and available to review before signing. There is no long-term
              volume commitment required. Centers may adjust their availability
              and participation at any time through the provider portal.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-green-600">
              <svg
                class="w-5 h-5 flex-shrink-0"
                fill="currentColor"
                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              >
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"></path>
              </svg>
              <span
                >No long-term volume commitment — adjust participation anytime</span
              >
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>

      <!-- FAQ 9 -->
      <details
        id="modalities"
        class="group bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow duration-300"
        data-aos="fade-up"
        data-aos-delay="400"
      >
        <summary
          class="flex justify-between items-center cursor-pointer p-6 hover:bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl transition-colors"
        >
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 pr-4">
            Which imaging modalities does USRad support?
          </h3>
          <div class="flex-shrink-0 ml-2">
            <svg
              class="w-6 h-6 text-gray-400 group-open:text-[#cc9933] group-open:rotate-180 transition-all duration-300"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <path
                stroke-linecap="round"
                stroke-linejoin="round"
                stroke-width="2"
                d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"></path>
            </svg>
          </div>
        </summary>
        <div class="px-6 pb-6">
          <div class="pt-4 border-t border-gray-100">
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              USRad currently supports MRI, CT, X-ray, and ultrasound at
              participating accredited facilities. Additional modalities may
              be confirmed during onboarding based on your center's equipment
              and accreditation.
            </p>
            <div class="mt-4 bg-blue-50 rounded-lg p-4">
              <p class="text-sm text-blue-800">
                <strong>Accreditation required</strong> — accredited by ACR, AIUM,
                IAC, The Joint Commission, or RadSite. Specific modality availability
                is confirmed during the credentialing process.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-12" data-aos="fade-up" data-aos-delay="450">
      <a
        href="/provider/faq"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[#003087] hover:text-[#cc9933] font-semibold transition-colors group"
      >
        <span>View all FAQs</span>
        <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
